
                        FPEXchange.rexx v1.0 by PMK.
                    Flux Point Amiga BBS  +45 3526 2527



  Introduction:
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~

  On my BBS I keep a 1:5 byte and file ratio, plus I give 10% bonus bytes to
the Uploader, each time his upload is downloaded! (Using CNet's build-in
features.) - However several of my good users sometimes run out of file
credits, but still having lot's of byte credits! - Here's the solution!

  FPExchange! - It allows the users to 'Exchange' some of their Byte Credits
into File Credits! - The 'price' of a file credit is based on the average byte
size the users has uploaded! (Uploaded Bytes / Uploaded Files = PRICE)

  The user has to have uploaded minimum 512K, called the board at least
10 times, and be really low on credits, as it will not allow a user to
have/buy more than 10 file credits! - These values can be changed by editing
the FPExchange.rexx program, and change the four variables at the start of 
the program.


  Installation:
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~

1) Copy FPEXchange.rexx to the pfiles: directory.


2) Add the following line in BBSMENU, under section '2; Available everywhere'

	FPEX		|   #0PFiles:FPExchange.rexx}





